  "verbalization": "Phellandral, (R)- is linked to Riboflavin synthase through multiple indirect pathways, with the most direct route involving the Sarcoplasmic/endoplasmic reticulum calcium ATPase 2, which is targeted by Milatuzumab. This suggests a potential mechanism where Phellandral, (R)- may modulate the activity of the calcium pump, influencing the cellular environment that affects Riboflavin synthase. The second pathway, involving the Colicin I receptor, points to a more complex interaction, possibly through a bacterial toxin that indirectly affects Riboflavin synthase. The third pathway, linking Phellandral, (R)- to UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B15, indicates a possible metabolic pathway where the compound may influence enzyme activity, which in turn could affect Riboflavin synthase. These findings suggest that Phellandral, (R)- may exert its effects through diverse mechanisms, potentially involving both direct and indirect interactions with cellular processes that ultimately influence Riboflavin synthase. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with the exact mechanism requiring further investigation.",
